Z||000000||Philphine||12-27-2001||08:12 AM||||<BR>since i'm scheduled to be active duty for the next year and pretty much all bases have gyms i'm gonna lose one excuse for not exercising. we even get 3 hours a week paid for physical fitness (subject to work load). <P>i'm pretty much happy with my weight (since my fav. physical activity thing is running [shut up sex fiends] i don't want to be big) but i'd like to be a little more solid. <P>doing some weights and situps and thinking about what i eat, but anbody got any tips or tricks that help them? especially calves. i've got skinny legs.   <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>ain't no place like home,<BR>ain't no place like home,<BR>ain't no place like home.||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||12-27-2001||09:59 AM||||Well, if you want to keep your general size but get more strength and more toned, the general rule is do to high reps and low weights on your exercises.  <BR>When I say high reps, for the most part I mean things like 3x15, or 2x20....things like that.  You really don't need to go alot higher on reps unless you are using super light weight.<P>As for your calves.  If there are not calf machines in your weight room.  Go to a squat rack and take some weight plates and lay them inside the rack, and then put some weight on the squat bar, and do your calve raises like that.  With calf exercises though, it's hard to do low reps and really get a good workout, but if you want to try to build your mass, I would suggest sets of 12-15.  But there really aren't alot of calfexercises besides that.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||12-27-2001||04:49 PM||||join an aerobics class so you can check out the chicks working out.<P><BR>i would start out with small weights, doing 3 sets of 8.  And try jogging in place for 5 minutes.  After you get sore the next day.  Dont do anything.  After that day, try increasing the weight and try getting 3 sets of 8.  And add running around the block once or twice, depending if your not too tired.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-27-2001||04:57 PM||||and if you want to have great legs like fierolisa,<P>try putting some weight on your shoulders, and while standing flat on your feet, push up on your toes(so your standing on your toes)  A heavy weight is ideal for this.  I would do this on a machine at school using triple digit weights.<P>Plus, you can work out your quads by having a weight on your shoulders and squating down and up.  Be sure NOT TO, go lower when your thigh is 90 degrees with the ceiling.  (squatting to low) cause it will damage your knees.  And keep your back straight performing this also, or back injury will result.<P>i would go to a store and get some weightlifting magazines, and they got pics of working out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||12-27-2001||06:05 PM||||Phil,No matter what you do,don't start off too hard.If you overdo it with your calfs,you may not be able to walk for a while because of the pain.||||reg||1
